take the photo during dolby vision and hlg recording from the hal stream

classes com/oplus/ocs/camera/producer/mode/VideoMode isVideoSnapShotByAps() sent every Dolby Vision / HLG session
to APS, which cuts the photo out of the 10-bit preview frame (QTI P010, 0x7fa30c0a). The OnePlus 9's APS
(/odm/lib64/libAlgoProcess.so) cannot JPEG-encode P010 ("swJpegWriteYUVData() not support format: 2141391882")
and every photo taken while recording came out green. Without that clause a 10-bit session takes the photo from
the HAL capture stream (video_recorder_snapshot_case), the same as plain 10-bit video does; with
com.oplus.photo.10bit.format = 35 in the odm camera config that stream is 8-bit YUV and APS encodes it.
VID20261021214440.mp4 (DOVI 8.4, HLG): photos at 21:44:42-44 1080x1920, mean U 126 V 132.

